Subject: [PATCH 3/9] port: adapt platform assumptions for WASIX

The sandbox has no root user to refuse, no host passwd database, no
`locale -a` to run, no setsid and no dynamic loading, and the
installation lives at mounted guest paths rather than a configured
prefix. Guard each assumption: skip the root check, report a fixed
wasix user, enumerate no system collations, stub dlopen to fail
cleanly, drop HAVE_SETSID, and resolve the share and pkglib
directories relative to the running binary's guest path.

diff --git a/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c b/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
index 8acbfbb..7be6d6f 100644
--- a/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
+++ b/src/backend/commands/collationcmds.c
@@ -575,7 +575,7 @@ pg_collation_actual_version(PG_FUNCTION_ARGS)
 
 
 /* will we use "locale -a" in pg_import_system_collations? */
-#if !defined(WIN32)
+#if !defined(WIN32) && !defined(__wasi__)
 #define READ_LOCALE_A_OUTPUT
 #endif
 
